    "text": "wdrb.com\nwebsite\nJefferson County, Kentucky\nJCPS breaks ground on new $30 million Kerrick Elementary School\nBy Joel Schipper,\n1 days agoLOUISVILLE, Ky. (WDRB) — Jefferson County Public Schools broke ground Tuesday on a new Kerrick Elementary, marking another step in the district’s long-term facilities plan. The new $30 million school will be built on Upper Hunter’s Trace, just behind the existing 70-year-old building, which will be demolished once...\n1",
